  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<section class=\"context\"><p>A moon M orbits a planet P. The graph shows the variation of the gravitational potential V<sub>g</sub> with distance r. The graph is drawn between the surface of M and the surface of P.</p>\n<p><br/></p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> Determine the gravitational field strength at r = 15 Mm. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> The distance between the centres of M and P is 19.6 Mm.</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b.i\"><p><strong>b.i</strong> Determine the radius of P. [1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b.ii\"><p><strong>b.ii</strong> </p><p>A spacecraft travels from the surface of P to the surface of M. The work done by the gravitational force on the spacecraft to reach M is –8.1 × 10<sup>10</sup> J.</p>\n<p>Calculate the mass of the spacecraft.</p><p>[2]</p></section>"
  },
